\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Transfer to A100} (bs=1, graph-timed, A100-SXM4-40GB --- the same GPU the harness constants were measured on). Left: fp16 latency predicted zero-shot from the model form plus \emph  {measured} A100 hardware constants --- nothing fitted to A100 kernel measurements. (An earlier draft read a slope break at $C_\text  {eff}$ into this curve; close numerical reading does not support that --- the marginal slope bumps near 32--40\nobreakspace  {}MB and settles, and the gate on this card is visible in the \emph  {relative} w8a8/bf16 structure, not in raw bf16 latency.) Right: the W4A16 Triton kernel after a two-point calibration of $(r_\text  {dequant},\ \text  {fixed cost})$ on the target; the dotted gray line scales H100 kernel terms by peak ratio and fails. Data: \texttt  {profiling/portable/results\_transfer\_a100.json}.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:transfer}{{2}{5}{\textbf {Transfer to A100} (bs=1, graph-timed, A100-SXM4-40GB --- the same GPU the harness constants were measured on). Left: fp16 latency predicted zero-shot from the model form plus \emph {measured} A100 hardware constants --- nothing fitted to A100 kernel measurements. (An earlier draft read a slope break at $C_\text {eff}$ into this curve; close numerical reading does not support that --- the marginal slope bumps near 32--40~MB and settles, and the gate on this card is visible in the \emph {relative} w8a8/bf16 structure, not in raw bf16 latency.) Right: the W4A16 Triton kernel after a two-point calibration of $(r_\text {dequant},\ \text {fixed cost})$ on the target; the dotted gray line scales H100 kernel terms by peak ratio and fails. Data: \texttt {profiling/portable/results\_transfer\_a100.json}.\relax }{figure.caption.18}{}}
